  "details": "Given how many different ways an avatar can be perceived, be it by having features blocked by shield settings, or impostors shown, or fallbacks, it is hard to get an idea of how you look to others when selecting an avatar.\n\nThis is also annoying when developing avatars, as it is hard to determine what the \"default\" look of the avatar you are creating is.\n\nMy suggestion is to add options to the personal mirror so it shows specific versions of the avatar. Since the avatar shown on the mirror is not a true reflection, but rather a clone of your avatar, I think it would be viable to change how it looks and behaves.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Setting the mirror to block custom animations\n\n- Setting the mirror to display the impostor avatar\n\n- Setting the mirror to a specific shield level\n\nI doubt that displaying cross-platform avatars is really viable this way (as in being able to see Android avatars in PC), but that would be an extra awesome option if possible.",
